  "id": "Compound::DB00471 - Disease::DOID:2841",
  "verbalization": "Montelukast and Asthma are linked through a shared biological pathway involving Leukotriene Receptor Antagonists. Both Montelukast and Zafirlukast, which are included in the class of Leukotriene Receptor Antagonists, are associated with treating Asthma. This relationship is supported by multiple evidence paths, which collectively indicate that Zafirlukast, a member of this class, has a therapeutic effect on Asthma. The evidence also highlights that Montelukast, as part of this pathway, is involved in the treatment of Asthma, reinforcing the connection between the drug and the condition. The lowest common ancestor of Montelukast and Zafirlukast is identified as the Carbonyl Compound, and both are classified as Anti-Asthmatic Agents, further supporting their role in the treatment of Asthma. The scores from the paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship between Montelukast and Asthma, though the strength of the evidence is slightly lower in Path 3 compared to the others.",
